[h1]About[/h1]
Standardised Country Colours is a cross-game project that assigns consistent, historically inspired map colours to selectable countries in various grand strategy games. This is the Victoria 3 edition, which applies the shared palette to supported countries, drawing it from established strategy-game palettes and national flags, so the world map reads clearly and each country keeps a recognisable colour.

[h1]Capabilities[/h1]
[list]
[*]Standardised map colours for all supported countries
[*]One shared palette, so neighbouring countries no longer share near-identical map colours
[*]Historically inspired and flag-derived colours, taken from established strategy-game palettes and national flags
[*]Colour-only overrides that leave tier, culture, capital, and every other country field to the base game
[*]Colours reapplied whenever a country is released or formed during a campaign
[*]No scripts, events, or saved state, so enabling or disabling the mod leaves a save untouched
[/list]

